      "explanation": "First calculate the exponents: \\(5^2=25\\) and \\(2^5=32\\). An odd power of \\(-1\\) equals \\(-1\\), and every positive integer power of \\(1\\) equals \\(1\\). Therefore\n\\[\n(-1)^{5^2}+1^{2^5}\n=(-1)^{25}+1^{32}\n=-1+1=\\boxed{0},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
